---
/**
 * The API reference, rendered by Stoplight Elements.
 *
 * `<elements-api>` is a web component, so it only runs in the browser: Stoplight fetches
 * `/openapi.json` itself and does its own routing, deep links and search. That is why this file is
 * nearly empty — the work is in having a correct spec at `/openapi.json`, which
 * `scripts/sync-openapi.mjs` guarantees, and in the custom element being registered, which
 * `Base.astro` does once for the whole site.
 *
 * The element carries no client directive. Astro's `client:*` resolve an *import*, and for a custom
 * element there is nothing to import but the registration already performed — so `client:load` here
 * fails the build with `NoMatchingImport`, an error that names the tag rather than the directive.
 */

/*
 * `router="hash"` matters more than it looks. Stoplight supports `hash` and `memory`, and `memory`
 * keeps its route in JS state — so a bookmarked `#/tag/Shipments/operation/create` breaks on reload,
 * and a link pasted into a ticket opens the overview instead of the operation. `hash` makes every
 * internal link a real, shareable URL.
 */
---

<elements-api apiDescriptionUrl="/openapi.json" layout="sidebar" router="hash" />
